Under SEBI (CRA) Regulations, 1999, every written agreement between a credit rating agency and its client must include:
- the rights and liabilities of each party;
- the fee to be charged;
- that the client shall co-operate for periodic review;
- that the client shall provide true, adequate and timely information;
- that the CRA shall disclose the rating assigned to the client's securities irrespective of whether the rating is accepted by the client;
- that the client shall disclose all ratings assigned in the last three years and any unaccepted rating;
- that the client shall obtain a rating for any issue of debt securities in accordance with the relevant regulations (originally, that the client shall agree to obtain a rating from at least two different rating agencies for any issue of debt securities whose size is equal to or exceeds, rupees one hundred crores, which was substituted by the SEBI (CRA) (Second Amendment) Regulations, 2011, w.e.f. 27-12-2011).
